sub_0205EE60: falls off the end for a1 > 4 ("UB: No return value"). The ROM
(unk_0205EC84.o: `cmp r1, #4; bhi <pop {r3, pc}>`) returns r0 unchanged,
i.e. the state pointer, which every caller reads as TRUE. wasm would return
an undefined value, so the ROM's value is returned explicitly.

--- a/arm9/src/unk_0205EC84.c
+++ b/arm9/src/unk_0205EC84.c
@@ -149,7 +149,8 @@
     case 4:
         return _flag_check(state, 0x96C);
     }
-    // UB: No return value
+    // UB: No return value. The ROM returns r0 untouched: the state pointer.
+    return (BOOL)(u32)state;
 }
 
 BOOL sub_0205EEB8(struct SaveVarsFlags *state, u32 a1) {
